(2770,	851,	'introduction',	'<article class=\"fh-activity-page\"><section class=\"fh-intro\">\r\n<h2>Discover Punta Cocos in Holbox</h2>\r\n<p class=\"fh-lead\">Quiet beaches, shallow turquoise water, spectacular sunsets and the\r\npossibility of seeing wild flamingos make Punta Cocos one of the most\r\nmemorable places to visit on Holbox Island.</p>\r\nLocated on the western side of Holbox, Punta Cocos offers a peaceful\r\nalternative to the beaches near the center of town. Its open coastline,\r\nnatural surroundings and relaxed atmosphere make it especially appealing\r\nto couples, families, photographers and nature lovers.\r\n\r\nVisitors can walk along the beach, enjoy the shallow water, observe local\r\nbirdlife and stay for one of the island’s most beautiful sunsets. Flamingo\r\nsightings depend on natural conditions and cannot be guaranteed, but the\r\nlandscape alone makes Punta Cocos worth visiting.\r\n\r\n</section><!-- QUICK FACTS -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-quick-facts\">\r\n<h2>Punta Cocos Quick Facts</h2>\r\n<div class=\"fh-facts-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">📍</span>\r\n<strong>Location</strong>\r\nWestern side of Holbox Island</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">🦩</span>\r\n<strong>Known For</strong>\r\nFlamingos, wildlife and sunsets</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">🌅</span>\r\n<strong>Best Time</strong>\r\nEarly morning or late afternoon</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">🎟️</span>\r\n<strong>Entrance</strong>\r\nFree public beach access</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">⏱️</span>\r\n<strong>Time Needed</strong>\r\nApproximately 1–2 hours</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-fact-card\"><span class=\"fh-fact-icon\">🛺</span>\r\n<strong>Getting There</strong>\r\nGolf cart, bicycle, taxi or walking</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- WHY VISIT -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-feature-row\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-feature-image\"><img src=\"PASTE-PUNTA-COCOS-IMAGE-URL\" alt=\"Flamingos and turquoise water at Punta Cocos in Holbox\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-feature-copy\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">A Peaceful Side of the Island</span>\r\n<h2>Why Visit Punta Cocos?</h2>\r\nPunta Cocos presents a very different atmosphere from the busier beaches\r\nnear Holbox Town. The landscape feels open, natural and peaceful, with\r\nshallow water stretching toward the horizon.\r\n\r\nIt is an excellent location for slowing down, taking photographs, walking\r\nalong the shoreline or simply enjoying the surrounding nature. Because the\r\nbeach faces west, it is also one of the most popular places in Holbox for\r\nwatching the sunset.\r\n<div class=\"fh-highlight-box\">\r\n\r\nPunta Cocos is especially beautiful in the early morning and during the\r\nfinal hours before sunset, when temperatures are cooler and the natural\r\nlight is softer.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- FLAMINGOS -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-feature-row fh-reverse\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-feature-image\"><img src=\"PASTE-PUNTA-COCOS-IMAGE-URL\" alt=\"Wild flamingos near Punta Cocos on Holbox Island\" /></div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-feature-copy\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Wildlife Experience</span>\r\n<h2>Flamingos at Punta Cocos</h2>\r\nPunta Cocos is one of several areas around Holbox where visitors may\r\noccasionally observe wild Caribbean flamingos. The birds are generally\r\nattracted to shallow areas where they can feed and rest.\r\n\r\nTheir presence varies according to water depth, food availability,\r\nweather, season and other natural conditions. For this reason, flamingo\r\nsightings should never be presented as guaranteed.\r\n\r\nWhen flamingos are present, observe them quietly from a respectful\r\ndistance. Avoid entering their feeding areas, approaching them for close\r\nphotographs or flying drones nearby.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- SUNSET AND ACTIVITIES -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section fh-tips-wrap\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Plan Your Visit</span>\r\n<h2>Things to Do at Punta Cocos</h2>\r\nPunta Cocos is more than a flamingo-viewing location. Visitors can enjoy the\r\nbeach throughout the day and experience a quieter side of Holbox.\r\n<div class=\"fh-tips-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Watch for flamingos and other local birdlife.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Walk along the peaceful western shoreline.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Enjoy the shallow water when conditions are suitable.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Photograph the beach and natural landscape.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Stay for one of Holbox’s best sunsets.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Visit after dark during suitable bioluminescence conditions.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- BEST TIME -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">When to Go</span>\r\n<h2>Best Time to Visit Punta Cocos</h2>\r\nEarly morning is a particularly pleasant time to visit. Temperatures are\r\nusually cooler, the beach is quieter and the soft light is ideal for\r\nlandscape and wildlife photography.\r\n\r\nLate afternoon is equally popular because Punta Cocos faces west and offers\r\nbeautiful sunset views. Arrive before sunset to allow enough time to explore\r\nthe beach and choose a comfortable viewing spot.\r\n\r\nBring insect repellent, especially around dusk and during humid periods.\r\nVisitors should also carry drinking water, sun protection and a flashlight\r\nwhen planning to return after dark.\r\n\r\n</section><!-- MAP -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-map-card\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-map-copy\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\" style=\"color: #f0c65e;\">Location</span>\r\n<h2>Where Is Punta Cocos?</h2>\r\nPunta Cocos is located west of Holbox Town. Travel time depends on your\r\nstarting point, current road conditions and your chosen transportation.\r\n\r\nOpen the location in Google Maps to plan your route from your hotel or\r\nfrom the center of Holbox.\r\n\r\n<a class=\"fh-button fh-button-white\" href=\"https://maps.app.goo.gl/RzHLPDycvu3nEeaw8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\r\nView Punta Cocos on Google Maps\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-map-visual\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Punta Cocos beach and flamingos in Holbox\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- HOW TO GET THERE -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Local Transportation</span>\r\n<h2>How to Get to Punta Cocos</h2>\r\nPunta Cocos can be reached from Holbox Town using several forms of local\r\ntransportation. Times vary according to your hotel location and the\r\ncondition of the island’s sandy roads.\r\n<div class=\"fh-transport-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-transport-card\">🛺\r\n<strong>Golf Cart</strong>\r\nConvenient for couples, families and small groups.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-transport-card\">🚲\r\n<strong>Bicycle</strong>\r\nA scenic option for active visitors.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-transport-card\">🚕\r\n<strong>Local Taxi</strong>\r\nArrange a return pickup when visiting after sunset.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-transport-card\">🚶\r\n<strong>Walking</strong>\r\nPossible from town, but allow extra time and carry water.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- VISITOR TIPS -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section fh-tips-wrap\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Helpful Information</span>\r\n<h2>Tips for Visiting Punta Cocos</h2>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tips-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Bring drinking water, sunscreen and insect repellent.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Wear shoes suitable for sand and shallow water.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Keep a respectful distance from all wildlife.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Never leave rubbish or plastic on the beach.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Do not rely on guaranteed flamingo sightings.</div>\r\n<div class=\"fh-tip\">Carry a flashlight when returning after dark.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- FAQ -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section fh-faq-wrap\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Frequently Asked Questions</span>\r\n<h2>Questions About Punta Cocos and Traveling to Holbox</h2>\r\nMost questions on this page should relate directly to Punta Cocos. One\r\nflight-related question is included because it helps visitors plan how to\r\nreach Holbox.\r\n\r\n<details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>Can you see flamingos at Punta Cocos?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nFlamingos may sometimes be seen in the shallow areas around Punta Cocos.\r\nTheir presence depends on weather, water levels, food availability and\r\nother natural conditions, so sightings cannot be guaranteed.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details><details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>What is the best time to visit Punta Cocos?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nEarly morning is ideal for cooler temperatures and a quieter beach.\r\nLate afternoon is popular for sunset views and warm photography light.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details><details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>Is Punta Cocos free to visit?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nPunta Cocos is a public beach and generally has free access.\r\nTransportation, rentals or private tours may involve additional costs.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details><details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>Can you swim at Punta Cocos?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nSwimming may be possible when sea and weather conditions are suitable.\r\nThe water is often shallow, but visitors should always assess current\r\nconditions before entering.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details><details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>How do I get from Holbox Town to Punta Cocos?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nYou can travel by rented golf cart, bicycle, local golf-cart taxi or on\r\nfoot. Travel time depends on your starting point and the condition of\r\nthe sandy roads.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details><details class=\"fh-faq-item\"><summary>What is the fastest way to travel from Cancun to Holbox?</summary>\r\n<div class=\"fh-faq-answer\">\r\n\r\nA private charter flight is the fastest option. Flights from Cancun to\r\nHolbox take approximately 30 minutes and arrive directly at Holbox\r\nAirport, avoiding the drive to Chiquilá and the ferry crossing.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</details></section><!-- RELATED ACTIVITIES -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-section\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\">Continue Exploring</span>\r\n<h2>More Things to Do in Holbox</h2>\r\n<div class=\"fh-related-grid\">\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<article class=\"fh-activity-card\"><img src=\"PASTE-BIOLUMINESCENCE-IMAGE-URL\" alt=\"Kayaking through bioluminescent water in Holbox\" />\r\n<div class=\"fh-card-overlay\">\r\n<h3>Bioluminescence in Holbox</h3>\r\nExperience glowing marine organisms during dark nighttime\r\nconditions around the island.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</article>&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<article class=\"fh-activity-card\"><img src=\"PASTE-WHALE-SHARK-IMAGE-URL\" alt=\"Swimming with a whale shark near Holbox\" />\r\n<div class=\"fh-card-overlay\">\r\n<h3>Whale Shark Tours</h3>\r\nLearn about seasonal whale shark excursions and what to expect\r\nduring this unforgettable experience.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</article>&nbsp;\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</section><!-- FLIGHTS HOLBOX CTA -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"fh-flight-cta\"><span class=\"fh-kicker\" style=\"color: #f0c65e;\">Flights Holbox</span>\r\n<h2>Fly to Holbox in Approximately 30 Minutes</h2>\r\nSkip the long drive and ferry journey. Flights Holbox offers private charter\r\nflights to Holbox from Cancun, Playa del Carmen, Cozumel, Mérida and Tulum.\r\n\r\nArrive directly on the island and spend more of your holiday exploring\r\nPunta Cocos and the natural beauty of Holbox.\r\n\r\n<a class=\"fh-button\" href=\"/contact-us/\">\r\nRequest Your Private Flight\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n</section></article>'),
